Hi, folks,

We have some problems in switching from VAX/VMS to Power Mac
related to key mappings.
The DEC keyboard contains many system specific keys like
the Gold Key, Do, Find, etc. and Mac doesn't, of course.
We have some database program called SmartStar running on VMS,
and it requires these keys - the keys on the right-hand-side 
section of keyboard - to be used.
When I use the NCSA telnet on Mac to connect to the VMS machine
and try to run the program, I simply can't because I don't
know which keys are equivalent to the ones I use on the DEC
keyboard.

Anyone out there know how to solve our problem? I won't mind 
getting new software if necessary, but preferably and hopefully,
I guess there might be some easier way.
I'm thinking of getting QuickKey for this, but wouldn't I
need ASCII codes for these keys anyway?

I'll really appreciate any kind of help about this.
If you respond by e-mail, please use the following address
because the one in the header of this posting is incorrect.



- Young Song
